column95:
Does a file containing one method need comments?<p><pre><code>  initialize: function(model_name, callback)
</code></pre>
It would be pretty pointless to add comments before every line of code like some people do:<p><pre><code>  // here is a for loop
    for (var i...)
  // declare a variable
    var x = 0;
</code></pre>
If there is supporting documentation about the operation of the method, which there is in that github page, then I fail to see what would be gained by adding verbose useless comments about typical code.
